hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"15800","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Suhayl ibn Abi Salih, from his father, from a man from Aslam, that he was stung and mentioned that to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Had you said in the evening: I seek refuge in the perfect words of Allah from the evil of what He created, it would not have harmed you. Suhayl said: My father, when one of us was stung, used to say: Did he say it? If they said yes, he said: As if he sees that it will not harm him."
